25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems the technical landscape is shifting; we have plenty of interest in modeling, but the experienced phenotyping technicians have largely migrated to industry.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've noticed that while computing costs are currently covered, the cost of animal-unit day rates has increased significantly, though glasshouse subsidies remain in place.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"The shared spectroscopy suite had a long outage last year, but the animal facility is now fully accredited with veterinary cover, though the glasshouses are completely full!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears that field-based work is currently a gamble, with several sites lost to disasters, and projects involving live breeding colonies are prone to significant delays.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"It is interesting to note that catalogue-style projects tend to provide lasting value, whereas mechanism-focused studies often conclude without resolving their primary questions.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,pass,Servas,,Skip,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Midori,,It is quite concerning that the costs are shifting so unevenly; we must consider how these financial pressures might impact the feasibility of the proposals.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"I wonder if we should be extra careful about any project that needs those glasshouses, since they're totally booked up!","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, the risk of environmental disruption combined with the volatility of breeding colonies suggests we should favor projects with more stable, perhaps computational, foundations.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Toshio,,I agree with Benjamin; the data suggests that stability and long-term utility are more reliable metrics than the initial promise of a complex mechanism.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must also remember that a project is only as strong as the hands that guide it; without the right technicians, even the most stable plan may falter.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree, Servas. We should be mindful of whether the proposed work relies on those specific technical skills that are now in short supply.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Kenji,,That's a great point! We should definitely check if the candidates need those phenotyping experts or if they can use the new modeling people instead!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A logical approach, then. We should prioritize candidates whose methodologies align with current staffing strengths and avoid those dependent on the dwindling pool of phenotyping specialists.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Precisely. We should seek a balance between long-term utility and operational feasibility, avoiding the pitfalls of both technical shortages and environmental instability.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Servas,,I believe we have gathered a comprehensive set of constraints to guide our final decision with wisdom and foresight.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Midori,,I feel we are all in agreement on the risks; now we just need to see which of the candidates fits these realities best.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm so excited to see who the candidates are! Let's hope there's one that fits everything we've talked about!,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I suspect the data will reveal a clear front-runner once we map these operational constraints against the specific requirements of each proposal.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I am ready to evaluate the candidates based on the evidence we have gathered.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
